# 5. Time and space complexity questions

This is one of the most important sections because your assignment specifically focuses on complexity analysis.

**Q18. What is the time complexity of recursive Fibonacci?**

O(2ⁿ), because the function makes repeated recursive calls.

**Q19. What is the space complexity of recursive Fibonacci?**

O(n), because the maximum depth of the recursive call stack is proportional to n.

**Q20. What is the time complexity of iterative Fibonacci?**

O(n), because the loop executes n times.

**Q21. What is the space complexity of iterative Fibonacci?**

O(1), when we store only the previous two numbers and the next calculated number.

**Q22. Which algorithm is faster?**

The iterative algorithm is generally faster because it avoids repeated calculations and recursive function-call overhead.

**Q23. What is exponential time complexity?**

It is a complexity in which the execution time grows exponentially as the input size increases.

**Q24. What is linear time complexity?**

It is a complexity in which execution time increases proportionally with input size.

**Q25. What is auxiliary space?**

Auxiliary space is the extra memory used by an algorithm, excluding the memory required for the input.

### Important complexity comparison

| Method | Time Complexity | Space Complexity |
|---|---|---|
| Recursive | O(2ⁿ) | O(n) |
| Iterative (optimized) | O(n) | O(1) |
| Dynamic Programming (array) | O(n) | O(n) |
